0,"quota":97.0,"prezzo":10.51,"variazione":3.2,"settimane_con_dati":4,"totale":false}]},"revisioni_recenti":[],"bollettino":[],"annotazioni":[],"rese":[{"etichetta":"Frozen whole, net of glaze","resa":100},{"etichetta":"Cleaned (tubes and tentacles)","resa":62}],"dimostrativo":false,"lede":"Squid imported into Italy closes week 46 at €10.18/kg, down 2.5% on the week. Against the same period of 2025 the price is 15.0% higher. For mid-November it is the highest level of the last three years. Over the last twelve months available, September 2025 to August 2026, Italy imported 60,706 tonnes, 17% of it from Morocco, down 4% on the previous twelve.","sintesi_html":"<section class=\"pir-riquadro pir-sintesi\" id=\"sintesi\">\n  <h2>Squid <b>at a glance</b></h2>\n  <p class=\"pir-lede\">Squid imported into Italy closes week 46 at €10.18/kg, down 2.5% on the week. Against the same period of 2025 the price is 15.0% higher. For mid-November it is the highest level of the last three years. Over the last twelve months available, September 2025 to August 2026, Italy imported 60,706 tonnes, 17% of it from Morocco, down 4% on the previous twelve.</p>\n  <table class=\"pir-tabella\">\n    <caption>Last twelve weeks. EUMOFA (European Commission), weekly EU imports from customs data.</caption>\n    <thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>€/kg</th><th>Tonnes</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody><tr><td>2026-W35</td><td>8.02</td><td>281</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W36</td><td>10.18</td><td>99</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W37</td><td>11.52</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W38</td><td>9.21</td><td>62</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W39</td><td>9.80</td><td>220</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W40</td><td>11.34</td><td>40</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W41</td><td>10.06</td><td>202</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W42</td><td>10.16</td><td>392</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W43</td><td>10.05</td><td>281</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W44</td><td>11.05</td><td>270</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W45</td><td>10.44</td><td>325</td></tr><tr><td>2026-W46</td><td>10.18</td><td>261</td></tr></tbody>\n  </table>\n  <table class=\"pir-tabella pir-provenienze\"><caption>Non-EU origins compared, volume-weighted average of weeks 43-46. Change is against the previous four weeks.</caption><thead><tr><th>Origin</th><th>€/kg</th><th>Change</th><th>Tonnes</th><th>Share</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"pir-totale\"><td>All origins</td><td>10.43</td><td>+3.2%</td><td>1,137</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td>Morocco</td><td>10.51</td><td>+3.2%</td><td>1,099</td><td>97%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n  <dl class=\"pir-domande\"><dt>What about flying squid?</dt><dd>It has its own customs codes and very different prices: this page covers only Loligo vulgaris squid, which customs identify separately. Keeping them apart is what makes the price readable.</dd><dt>Is this the price I pay my supplier?</dt><dd>No. It is the average value declared at customs by importers into Italy, across all sizes. Use it to compare your own purchase price with the average and to read the trend, not as a quotation.</dd><dt>How up to date is it?</dt><dd>The data come out every week and run to about two weeks earlier: the most recent week is always incomplete at the source and is published only once it is closed.</dd></dl>\n</section>"}